  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#dom-img-decode\r\n\r\nIt seems a bit odd that `img.decode()` is a no-op for vector images, especially as it was compared to `createImageBitmap(img)` which does create bitmap data from vector images.\r\n\r\nThe image could be decoded to its `.width` and `.height` – this may also be useful for non-vector progressive formats, as additional scans could be skipped.\r\n\r\nBrowser dev tools could warn if the `.decode()` wasn't used, eg because it decoded to the wrong size.",
